      "summaries": {
        "en": "MeTube is a self-hosted web application that solves the problem of downloading YouTube videos without relying on external services, giving users full control over their media collection. It works by providing a clean web interface that wraps powerful command-line tools like yt-dlp, making complex downloading operations accessible through simple clicks. You can deploy it on your own server using Docker, then use it to download videos in various formats, create playlists, or archive educational content for offline access and personal use.",
        "zh": "MeTube是一款自托管的网络应用，它解决了用户依赖外部服务下载YouTube视频的问题，让用户能够完全掌控自己的媒体收藏。该项目通过简洁的网页界面封装了yt-dlp等强大命令行工具，将复杂的下载操作转化为直观的点击操作，降低了技术门槛。部署时只需使用Docker在个人服务器上运行，即可用来下载多种格式的视频、创建播放列表，或存档教育内容供离线学习使用，特别适合需要批量管理视频资源的场景。",
        "es": "MeTube is a self-hosted web application that solves the problem of downloading YouTube videos without relying on external services, giving users full control over their media collection. It works by providing a clean web interface that wraps powerful command-line tools like yt-dlp, making complex downloading operations accessible through simple clicks. You can deploy it on your own server using Docker, then use it to download videos in various formats, create playlists, or archive educational content for offline access and personal use.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "metube stands out for self-hosted, youtube, and youtube-dl in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "MeTube is a self-hosted web application that solves the problem of downloading YouTube videos without relying on external services, giving users full control over their media collection. It works by providing a clean web interface that wraps powerful command-line tools like yt-dlp, making complex downloading operations accessible through simple clicks. You can deploy it on your own server using Docker, then use it to download videos in various formats, create playlists, or archive educational content for offline access and personal use.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/alexta69/metube for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
