      "summaries": {
        "en": "Handy is an open-source speech-to-text application that enables reliable offline transcription, addressing privacy concerns and connectivity limitations. Built with TypeScript and Tauri v2, it leverages efficient local processing to deliver cross-platform accessibility without cloud dependencies. Developers can extend its functionality through plugins, while users benefit from customizable workflows for real-time captioning, note-taking, or accessibility tools in diverse environments.",
        "zh": "Handy是一款开源离线语音转文字应用，通过本地化处理解决隐私和网络依赖问题，让转录更安全可靠。它基于TypeScript和Tauri v2框架实现跨平台运行，核心设计在于利用轻量级本地引擎替代云端服务，兼顾效率与可扩展性。用户可将其用于实时字幕生成、会议记录或辅助工具，开发者也能通过插件机制定制功能，适合需要离线、可定制转录场景的实践探索。",
        "es": "Handy is an open-source speech-to-text application that enables reliable offline transcription, addressing privacy concerns and connectivity limitations. Built with TypeScript and Tauri v2, it leverages efficient local processing to deliver cross-platform accessibility without cloud dependencies. Developers can extend its functionality through plugins, while users benefit from customizable workflows for real-time captioning, note-taking, or accessibility tools in diverse environments.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "Handy stands out for accessibility, cross-platform, and speech-to-text in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Handy is an open-source speech-to-text application that enables reliable offline transcription, addressing privacy concerns and connectivity limitations. Built with TypeScript and Tauri v2, it leverages efficient local processing to deliver cross-platform accessibility without cloud dependencies. Developers can extend its functionality through plugins, while users benefit from customizable workflows for real-time captioning, note-taking, or accessibility tools in diverse environments.",
